From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DannyBaanks <danny@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:07:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Linux: TLS ABI, atomic saves, live framebuffer, PipeWire
 audio, input pipe, and Vulkan floor

Implements Linux guest TLS slot ABI (linux_tls.c + patch_nso.py HOST_ABI 1), recursive directory clonefile() with copy fallback for atomic ext4 save transactions, portable NVN framebuffer replay + double-buffered shared-memory presenter (DM_FB_SHM) and PPM screenshots, non-blocking PipeWire/ALSA PCM audio streaming (DM_AUDIO_PIPE + audio_pcm.c), live input FIFO + evdev input, KMS mode probing, and the Vulkan execution/replay floor.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Enables end-to-end playable Switch execution on Linux (aarch64 native and x86_64 via QEMU) with live video, audio, controls, and atomic saves.
Issue: DannyBaanks/NX2Apple#1
